Mplus VERSION 9 DEMO (Mac)
MUTHEN & MUTHEN
10/17/2026  11:51 PM

INPUT INSTRUCTIONS

  DATA: FILE = standardize.dat;
  VARIABLE:
   NAMES = id y1 y2 y3 y4;
   USEVARIABLES = y1 y2 y3 y4;
   IDVARIABLE = id;
   CLASSES = c(3);
  DEFINE: STANDARDIZE y1 y2 y3 y4;
  ANALYSIS: TYPE = MIXTURE; STARTS = 200 40; STSEED = 20261017;
   MITERATIONS = 10000;
   LOGCRITERION = 0.00000001; RLOGCRITERION = 0.000000001;
   MCONVERGENCE = 0.000001;
  MODEL:
   %OVERALL%
   %c#1%
   [y1-y4]; y1-y4;
   %c#2%
   [y1-y4]; y1-y4;
   %c#3%
   [y1-y4]; y1-y4;
  SAVEDATA: FILE = standardize-posteriors.dat; SAVE = CPROBABILITIES; FORMAT = F20.12;
   RESULTS = standardize-results.dat;



*** WARNING in MODEL command
  All variables are uncorrelated with all other variables within class.
  Check that this is what is intended.
   1 WARNING(S) FOUND IN THE INPUT INSTRUCTIONS




